upstream: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/greensock/gsap-skills/main/skills/gsap-scrolltrigger/SKILL.md
verified: 2026-08-16
scope: directory
reason: upstream has a real bug — local fixes it
note: Line 235 of upstream reads:
  xPercent: () => Max.max(0, window.innerWidth - scrollingEl.offsetWidth),
  `Max` is not a JS global; this throws ReferenceError at runtime. Local
  (SKILL.md line ~236) fixes it to Math.max, reframes the calc as
  scrollWidth - clientWidth (the actual horizontal overflow, guarded at 0),
  makes `end` track that same distance instead of a fixed "+=1000", and adds
  invalidateOnRefresh: true so the computed values re-run on resize.
  Diffed 2026-08-16: upstream 296 lines, local 301 lines, this is the only
  functional divergence.
would_lose_if_wired: an unguarded byte-for-byte refresh would overwrite the
  working fork with upstream's broken Max.max(...) recipe.
refresh_guard: _refresh-vendored.sh skips this directory when .local-fork is
  present, before any fetch or write.

external_status: https://github.com/greensock/gsap-skills/issues/18 was observed
  open on 2026-08-16, filed by ongkipro with this defect and replacement.
  This task performed no external write or publication.

  Filing surfaced a point the earlier draft had missed, and it is the reason
  the local fork rewrites the snippet rather than patching one word: correcting
  `Max.max` to `Math.max` does not make upstream's version work. Horizontal
  scrolling means offsetWidth > innerWidth, so `innerWidth - offsetWidth` is
  negative and the `Math.max(0, ...)` clamp yields 0 — the tween animates to
  xPercent: 0, silently, with no error. The clamp also makes a negative value
  impossible, so the content can never move left at all. Separately, a pixel
  count is being assigned to `xPercent`, which is a percentage of the element's
  own width. So a one-word upstream fix would close the ReferenceError without
  closing the defect, and re-wiring .source on that basis would still lose the
  working recipe.

to_vendor: watch https://github.com/greensock/gsap-skills/issues/18. Remove the
  fork only when upstream's snippet actually moves the element — a `Math.max`
  typo fix alone is NOT sufficient (see above). Confirm with a re-diff, not
  merely with the issue being closed.

recheck: 2026-08-16 — still present upstream at line 235.
    curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/greensock/gsap-skills/main/skills/gsap-scrolltrigger/SKILL.md | grep -n 'Max\.max'
